  "At easier levels, move slowly until you learn the movement.": "På lettere nivåer, flytt sakte til du lærer bevegelsen.",
  "At least 120 min of scheduled Zone 2 and about 51 min of hard cardio a week; controlled vigorous blocks on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday.": "Minst 120 minutter med planlagt sone 2 og ca. 51 minutter hard cardio i uken; kontrollerte kraftige blokker tirsdag, torsdag og lørdag.",
  "At New to training and Returning, keep the pace brisk and below all-out effort. At Active, work hard. At Well trained, use all-out effort.": "At New to training and Returning, hold tempoet høyt og under all-out innsats. At Active, jobb hardt. At Well trained, bruk all-out innsats.",
  "At Returning and above, hold a dumbbell in each hand, or loop a band around your waist with its anchor in front of you. The band should pull you forward, like a sled.": "At Returning and above, hold en manual i hver hånd, eller løkke et bånd rundt midjen med ankeret foran deg. Bandet skal trekke deg fremover, som en slede.",
  "At Returning, push back up with your hands. At higher levels, pull yourself back with your hamstrings.": "At Returning, skyv opp igjen med hendene. At higher levels, trekk deg tilbake med hamstrings.",
  "At the end of your last interval, note your peak heart rate. Walk gently for 60 seconds and note your heart rate again. Enter the drop (peak minus 60s reading).": "På slutten av det siste intervallet, noter topppulsen din. Gå forsiktig i 60 sekunder og noter pulsen igjen. Gå inn i fallet (topp minus 60-tallets lesing).",
